==Strategy==
This stage is an exact copy of [[Honey Trap (Deadly)|Honey Trap]], though with a restriction in place. Due to the restriction, the player can no longer rely on [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] or expensive [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] to win the battle. Despite that, nothing much should change, as the original stage favoured disposable units anyways.

==='''Key Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier completely stomps this stage. He is too fast, has way too much damage, and way too short of a cooldown for anything in this stage to pose a threat. A level 31 Courier can tank a Brollow hit, while a level 40 Courier (or a level 36 Courier alongside a small Attack combo) can two-shot the Brollows.
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]]: Your primary meatshields, as their high speed allows them to get in Queen B's blindspot very easily. Note that a Crazed Tank at level 28 is able to tank a Brollow hit.
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]: In its True Form, Catellite has Slow Immune, allowing it to easily get inside Queen B's blindspot. Its Strong vs. Alien ability allows it to tank more hits from Kroxo as well as even get a bit of chip against a Kroxo if so needed. Catellite should be your third meatshield if you need one, after the Crazed meatshields. A level 34 Catellite, or a level 31 Catellite with a Defense combo is able to tank a Brollow hit.

==='''Useful Units'''===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can has very high base stats, allowing it to one-shot a Brollow or Kroxo, as well as being able to get strong hits off against THE SLOTH. Having access to Can Can's [[Talents]] makes it much better here, especially Move Speed Up, but an untalented Can Can is still very useful here.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Fishman's high stats and speed, especially given their Massive Damage vs. Floating, allows them to one shot Brollow and get huge chip damage against Queen B. Butterfly is also incredibly easy to time into Queen B's blindspot. You can use Butterfly Cat if you don't have the resources to True Form them, but getting their True Form for more Speed greatly improves their performance.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]]/[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]]: Sadako's high base health and Resistant vs. Floating allows it to serve as a strong wall against a horde of Brollows. Cleanerbot does the same thing, but can tank hits from THE SLOTH, making them just as valuable even if more feeble against the Brollow hordes.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]: Maglev can kill a single peon and grant you Extra Money for its kill. Maglev is good for stopping Queen B from pushing just after THE SLOTH attacks.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most Uber Rares from [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] are still usable here thanks to their low cost. Units such as [[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibon]] or [[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Volta]], if able to sneak through Queen B's hit, can get high value by getting either pure damage or CC against Queen B herself.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: You'll need either good timing or the usage of the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] cannon to sneak into Queen B's blindspot, but he is able to dish out ridiculously high damage when allowed in.
*Most rusher Ubers already have a low cost, so they aren't affected much by the restriction. Examples include [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]], [[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]], [[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]], and [[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Issun Boshi]].
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]]: DLuna targets every single trait present in this stage, can Weaken Brollows and THE SLOTH, has very high base stats, and is Slow Immune, essentially guaranteeing you a free win.

