'''Battle:''' Stall Queen B on the enemy base with Catellite and Fishman until the first Brollow wave. Lure the Brollows to the Cat Base, and start spamming Octopus Cats, Can Can Cats and Fishman Cats. You'll want to wedge a Vendor Cat into Queen B's blind spot after this. When done correctly, THE SLOTH should now be pushed behind Queen B; your units will have full rein to start damaging the boss, eventually pushing her back a good distance. At this point, try and get Worker Cat to ~level 6 and play defensively up until the third major wave of Brollows is exhausted. Reserve Maglev to retain your ground when THE SLOTH attacks and during the Brollow waves. Your Can Can Cats will find it difficult to enter Queen B's blind spot without their Move Speed Up Talent, so it is recommended to unlock it if possible.

